":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.8.dev.custom_build [e7cfa294a]\n- Reproducible in v4.5.2.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev (e7cfa294a) - Manjaro Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 04 Sep 2026 15:41:39 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors (1920x1080 @ 74.97 Hz, 1920x1080 @ 74.97 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7900 XT (RADV NAVI31) - AMD Ryzen 9 7900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads) - 30.48 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn an X11 project, when you have a maximized window set to always on top, disabling always on top also unmaximizes the window.\nIf the DisplayServer is set to Wayland, the issue does not occur.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Download the MRP below\n- Launch the project (on Wayland, if running from the editor, run it as a floating window without the toolbar, so it can spawn windows properly)\n- Click the button to open a new window\n- Press the space bar to toggle the new window's always-on-top flag\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[always-on-top-x11.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33021282/always-on-top-x11.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","r